## 4. Custom GLSL & TSL Shader Standards
When creating organic motion, liquid distortion, terrain, or interactive hover ripples:
- **Never** deform high-poly meshes on the CPU inside `useFrame`. Offload vertex displacement to custom GLSL vertex shaders (using 3D Simplex/Curl noise) or `three-custom-shader-material` so PBR lighting/shadows still react accurately to displaced vertices.
- **Standard Uniforms:** Always pass `uTime`, `uMouse` (lerped 2D/3D vector), `uScrollProgress` (`0.0` to `1.0`), and `uVelocity`.
- **Interactive Fluidity:** Smooth all mouse/pointer uniforms using exponential decay (`THREE.MathUtils.damp`) rather than raw pointer coordinates so shaders feel weighted and liquid.

